# Act Secrets Setup

RULE: Quickmerge runs act to simulate CI locally. Act needs GH_PAT to clone sibling repos (e.g. unified-trading-codex). Without it, act fails and quickmerge aborts.

WHY: Workflows clone sibling repos via secrets.GH_PAT. No token = act cannot run; quickmerge fails with a clear suggestion.

SSOT: unified-trading-pm/docs/repo-management/act-secrets-setup.md

## Setup (one-time)

1. `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/workspace/generate-act-secrets.sh`
2. Edit `<workspace-root>/.act-secrets` and add `GH_PAT=ghp_xxx`
3. Re-run quickmerge

## When act fails

Quickmerge exits 1 and prints the fix. Do not skip — fix the secrets. Use `--quick` only when intentionally skipping act.

## DO

- Run generate-act-secrets.sh once, fill in GH_PAT manually
- Keep .act-secrets at workspace root (gitignored)
- Re-run quickmerge after fixing secrets

## NEVER

- Commit .act-secrets or GH_PAT
- Suggest "just use --quick" when act fails due to missing secrets — point user to act-secrets-setup.md
